# Agent/editor config carries credentials and machine-local paths. Tracked
# copies leaked a provider bearer token (security audit finding
# opencode.json.committed-bearer-token-thehive-ai) and a developer home path;
# the committed *.example files are the portable shape.
opencode.json
.kilo/kilo.json
# Localhost demo stack state + logs (Wave 47 lane B1 scripts/demo-up.sh)
.demo-up/

# The object store the demo attachments are written into (scripts/e2e-stack.sh
# and scripts/demo-up.sh both name OBJECT_STORE_LOCAL_DIR). Seeded attachment
# bytes land here, so a stack boot is enough to populate it — it must never be
# tracked, or the demo org's objects get committed as repo files. `**/` so it
# matches at any depth: `cargo test -p core-api` runs with the crate dir as cwd,
# dropping the store at crates/core-api/data/objects/ (Wave 47 lane A7). Nothing
# under a data/objects path is tracked anywhere, so the wider pattern is safe.
**/data/objects/

# Shared cargo target dir (agent worktree build cache)
.kilo/target-shared/
# Lane-drifted private target caches (DX6 violation artifacts, reclaimed at merge)
.kilo/target-shared*/

# P13 build-throughput overlay: written per machine by scripts/p13-build-env.sh
# from what that host actually has (linker, sccache). Tracked config includes it
# with `optional = true`, so an absent copy is stock cargo — which is why it must
# never be committed: a committed copy would pin one machine's linker on every
# other machine. scripts/p13-build-env.sh selftest proves the include/absent pair.
.cargo/p13-fast.local.toml
# sccache's local cache, placed beside the shared target dir (one per machine).
.kilo/sccache/

# Graphify knowledge graph (machine-generated; hooks rebuild it locally)
graphify-out/

graphify-out

# Archify diagram output (agent-generated, regenerable). The skill writes one
# timestamped folder per request: the authoring candidate, the rendered HTML
# (hundreds of KB), the finalize/delivery/browser-check receipts, and any
# `review-N/` reruns. Same rule as `graphify-out/` and `website/public/docs/`:
# machine output is not tracked. A diagram worth keeping is promoted by hand
# (candidate plus HTML) into `design/` or `docs/reference/` and reviewed like
# any other artifact, so the repo carries the ones we mean to keep.
.archify/

# Stale pre-DX10 build dir (accidentally committed; artifacts live in .kilo/target-shared)
target-dx11/
lockfile: package-lock.json

packages/sdk/package-lock.json

# Desktop shell (ADR 0005): placeholder frontendDist + bundled resources
desktop/resources/
apps/web/out/

# The graft map's cache — regenerable, not committed (run `trail build`).
# Trail keeps it at `.trail/cache/` (ignored by `.trail/.gitignore`); a checkout
# with no committed `.trail/` wiring falls back to this top-level `graft/` dir.
/graft/

